. Fry has raised over $1.7 million and holds more than $1 million on hand, while Democrat John Vincent has raised under $300,000. Prediction markets give Vincent roughly a 6% chance of winning. The only public poll, conducted for a Democratic sponsor in late July, showed Fry ahead by four points, but its sponsor and the district's lean make it a weak signal. Fry is simultaneously running for the U.S. Senate special election, which has drawn attention but does not appear to have materially changed the House race. The race remains rated Likely Republican, with Fry expected to win by a comfortable but not overwhelming margin.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0379, "margin": -13.69}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0396, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0447, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0469, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0326, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0257, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.036, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -15.0}]}